  'Macroeconomics',
  'Macroeconomics',
  'This course follows a ten-unit sequence on national income, inflation and unemployment, aggregate demand and supply, fiscal and monetary policy, money and banking, long-run growth, business cycles, international trade, and open-economy macroeconomics.',
  $macrojson${"slug": "macroeconomics", "title": "Macroeconomics", "description": "This course follows a ten-unit sequence on national income, inflation and unemployment, aggregate demand and supply, fiscal and monetary policy, money and banking, long-run growth, business cycles, international trade, and open-economy macroeconomics.", "topics": [{"id": "4989cd8c-2e2d-4f5a-bd9a-0e611bef7efb", "type": "topic", "title": "National Income Accounting: GDP, GNP, GNI, and Macro Data", "description": "This unit teaches students how economists measure the size and composition of an economy. It turns broad claims about the economy into concrete, comparable indicators.", "children": [{"id": "19985e6c-9d08-4b9f-8902-33522051dea2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "GDP and output measurement", "children": [{"id": "27228acf-f7ad-4d1f-ae7a-0b6a77ab2da0", "type": "concept", "title": "Final goods and services"}, {"id": "2a58bb27-0906-43f2-9058-2fcc6201d76e", "type": "concept", "title": "Market value and production within borders"}, {"id": "3ab60089-65ee-49cd-ace2-409cdf395277", "type": "concept", "title": "Expenditure approach: C + I + G + NX"}, {"id": "9f3a8e9b-1410-4fb6-ae8d-6e3ea30e47c0", "type": "concept", "title": "Value-added approach"}], "description": "Students learn what GDP counts and why it is the central measure of production. The gist is that GDP is useful but incomplete."}, {"id": "0f50c16d-5f23-4e38-a571-65121851b20b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "GNP, GNI, and income concepts", "children": [{"id": "39023a97-8bcc-435c-b750-eba6a2acc93e", "type": "concept", "title": "Gross national product"}, {"id": "5defdd57-2ab0-4e94-b896-dee62c21f31a", "type": "concept", "title": "Gross national income"}, {"id": "51c73817-09ab-4678-8372-db4a67237f9c", "type": "concept", "title": "Net factor income from abroad"}, {"id": "a67f31af-a9a9-41c9-baf1-4298ffa4ae47", "type": "concept", "title": "Why multinational activity complicates measurement"}], "description": "These measures clarify the difference between production in a place and income earned by a country's residents. This matters for global business and cross-country comparison."}, {"id": "5dbbda53-a332-4132-ba20-eeb1b3e3bfa7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Nominal versus real values", "children": [{"id": "84fe6b95-73ab-4229-bb57-4470d5b83344", "type": "concept", "title": "Nominal GDP"}, {"id": "904abebc-5396-48de-ac52-7f921a7759b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Real GDP"}, {"id": "93b73424-0074-424c-887b-55990b56efed", "type": "concept", "title": "GDP deflator"}, {"id": "a3c72f74-d843-4dc3-b31d-f7a763330cc9", "type": "concept", "title": "Base years and index numbers"}], "description": "Students learn to separate price changes from quantity changes. This is the key to interpreting growth over time."}, {"id": "682ef01d-a67a-474d-b43a-98704f1d595e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Using macro data responsibly", "children": [{"id": "40418492-cd26-4af2-a68a-59bb32277551", "type": "concept", "title": "Per-capita measures"}, {"id": "50727d4f-3079-4f52-ae5a-2420a2a085e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Seasonal adjustment"}, {"id": "0ba052c1-3e3c-43d3-812a-a784883d6514", "type": "concept", "title": "Data revisions"}, {"id": "59e26f5e-19fa-4eb1-aa6f-306acabd72e0", "type": "concept", "title": "Limits of GDP: household work, inequality, environment, and well-being"}], "description": "Macro data are estimates built from definitions, surveys, and revisions. Students learn to read data with precision rather than false certainty."}]}, {"id": "5db4a939-790b-4f6b-8327-f867cfddd02b", "type": "topic", "title": "Inflation, CPI, Unemployment, and the Phillips Curve", "description": "This unit covers the macro indicators people feel most directly: prices and jobs. Students learn how inflation and unemployment are measured and why they create policy tradeoffs.", "children": [{"id": "49c1eec0-79f0-4022-baae-9b75ead9ab0e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inflation and price indexes", "children": [{"id": "e6a56d32-7aca-4ffa-8297-4739880ab27e", "type": "concept", "title": "Consumer Price Index"}, {"id": "db3ca5d4-448a-49ea-93f5-e0de96de83b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Producer Price Index"}, {"id": "efe181bd-dda0-4b3e-a250-7a777212f024", "type": "concept", "title": "GDP deflator"}, {"id": "21302598-9cff-4e23-a959-58625b6f4dcb", "type": "concept", "title": "Core versus headline inflation"}], "description": "Inflation measures the rate at which the general price level rises. The point is to distinguish broad inflation from changes in one price."}, {"id": "900b940d-d3f5-435e-9867-afd70beafd5e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Costs and causes of inflation", "children": [{"id": "696bb649-0d88-49f5-8c57-46a41ff2e0c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Purchasing power"}, {"id": "172953e2-6c50-4e31-a818-fd6e142ec824", "type": "concept", "title": "Menu costs and shoe-leather costs"}, {"id": "3ebb4eac-89e9-420e-abb3-7f00201a2eb8", "type": "concept", "title": "Unexpected inflation and debtors/creditors"}, {"id": "ee75b16c-750f-4676-a66a-99ed5a044023", "type": "concept", "title": "Demand-pull and cost-push inflation"}], "description": "Students learn why inflation matters even when wages and prices both change. The gist is that inflation redistributes purchasing power and can distort decisions."}, {"id": "62e7ae01-3e30-46eb-871e-f199694ae240", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Unemployment measurement", "children": [{"id": "15de7f0b-c503-403c-aeb1-989c6a2437d7", "type": "concept", "title": "Labor force"}, {"id": "e5b7fdaa-1aa2-4fc8-a32e-cd4713613036", "type": "concept", "title": "Unemployment rate"}, {"id": "3e30b7c4-4ff3-44e8-9013-fa8d5b7284f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Labor force participation"}, {"id": "e793fcd8-9e0c-4a90-989d-fea9da802b79", "type": "concept", "title": "Underemployment and discouraged workers"}], "description": "Unemployment is a labor-market indicator, but it is not as simple as counting people without jobs. Students learn the definitions behind the headline rate."}, {"id": "126055f3-332d-4124-a39a-4be9783ae09e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Phillips curve intuition", "children": [{"id": "ce9f0dfe-fb2d-4b31-973f-c0c1e2498faf", "type": "concept", "title": "Short-run Phillips curve"}, {"id": "b75e9c22-e9f3-4cbd-89c1-61589f9dc364", "type": "concept", "title": "Inflation expectations"}, {"id": "67e88280-dc78-411d-a428-1333cd27fcbd", "type": "concept", "title": "Natural rate of unemployment"}, {"id": "e8f23e89-933b-4bfa-981f-0d29e5ed6dd3", "type": "concept", "title": "Stagflation as a challenge to simple tradeoffs"}], "description": "The Phillips curve introduces the relationship between inflation and unemployment. Students learn why the short-run tradeoff can shift when expectations change."}]}, {"id": "df4887ce-6a1e-4f51-8766-fb5a81b3cd7d", "type": "topic", "title": "Aggregate Demand and Aggregate Supply", "description": "This unit gives students the main framework for analyzing economy-wide fluctuations. It shows how spending, production capacity, prices, and output interact.", "children": [{"id": "61cfe082-8a60-413e-bf16-a29a57db0b15", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Aggregate demand", "children": [{"id": "164372f4-4a67-4274-933e-22e80e3c56ef", "type": "concept", "title": "Components of AD"}, {"id": "1fee2694-2c7f-484d-b1ac-4b105cc90069", "type": "concept", "title": "Wealth effect"}, {"id": "79dd4de4-0a63-4ac9-9643-bbafa55780d2", "type": "concept", "title": "Interest-rate effect"}, {"id": "3132d52a-d59d-4e5c-b42d-7903584bf77d", "type": "concept", "title": "Exchange-rate effect"}], "description": "Aggregate demand represents planned spending across the economy. Students learn why consumption, investment, government spending, and net exports move together with the price level."}, {"id": "fca2bac8-f10c-4b76-94cb-e15e71942194", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Short-run aggregate supply", "children": [{"id": "065c5072-cee3-45b1-9191-57127ae562a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Sticky wages and prices"}, {"id": "b3dcede2-5c9b-4f53-8c89-2f4bf4f6851e", "type": "concept", "title": "Input costs"}, {"id": "c2da711b-1ddd-4232-b56a-d350ebec3010", "type": "concept", "title": "Productivity shocks"}, {"id": "58687974-8175-4350-95d1-63dd22690c5e", "type": "concept", "title": "Supply shocks"}], "description": "Short-run aggregate supply explains why output can rise or fall with prices before wages and expectations fully adjust."}, {"id": "88d50c00-4619-457c-a009-57a346cd9cc1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Long-run aggregate supply", "children": [{"id": "9b256e70-8539-4e72-8872-c3e233b3941b", "type": "concept", "title": "Potential GDP"}, {"id": "53f798dd-24e9-4879-a169-29fa928d3d6a", "type": "concept", "title": "Full-employment output"}, {"id": "86188d4d-b46b-4e00-9362-a3ce8b75c5cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Natural rate concepts"}, {"id": "9c8d239a-c48c-4da2-b550-9bd081b8df87", "type": "concept", "title": "Shifts from labor, capital, technology, and institutions"}], "description": "Long-run supply reflects productive capacity rather than short-run demand. Students learn the difference between temporary fluctuations and potential output."}, {"id": "f8c253b4-17d4-48c3-9b23-96b3637268be", "type": "subtopic", "title": "AD-AS equilibrium", "children": [{"id": "394012ca-85a2-4f0b-bfaf-ecd23148d6c2", "type": "concept", "title": "Short-run equilibrium"}, {"id": "d61121d1-a827-4580-bbc0-16f0ddb0c251", "type": "concept", "title": "Recessionary gap"}, {"id": "5d21e90e-396e-42a7-ac1c-c44acc1d57d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Inflationary gap"}, {"id": "5a0e3387-a3a8-40c3-969f-3fd252e4140d", "type": "concept", "title": "Demand shocks versus supply shocks"}], "description": "The AD-AS model connects inflation, unemployment, growth, and policy in one diagram. Students use it to reason through recessions, booms, and shocks."}]}, {"id": "e37bf733-3870-4bfd-9846-f3810938a5da", "type": "topic", "title": "Fiscal Policy and Government Budgets", "description": "Fiscal policy shows how government spending and taxation influence aggregate demand, distribution, debt, and long-run capacity. Students learn both the power and constraints of budget policy.", "children": [{"id": "b11d4ef1-256e-4353-b8c6-880333f8e115", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Government spending and taxes", "children": [{"id": "e6a3136a-cf0f-465b-bb50-10a96dd3ac80", "type": "concept", "title": "Government purchases"}, {"id": "8adb8440-f268-44c4-b59d-1499821979d3", "type": "concept", "title": "Transfers"}, {"id": "f82320db-a3eb-4512-b724-37e04072dc77", "type": "concept", "title": "Tax rates and tax bases"}, {"id": "c4b52ef5-6076-4a8e-b41e-4c5e78e08ba6", "type": "concept", "title": "Automatic stabilizers"}], "description": "Students learn the main tools of fiscal policy. The gist is that changes in spending and taxes alter demand and incentives."}, {"id": "c30f47a4-95fd-41a6-87b3-51927c8ac9cf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Multipliers", "children": [{"id": "13e0b6df-8c67-4ddc-9d11-54cbe2f76031", "type": "concept", "title": "Marginal propensity to consume"}, {"id": "616f3080-e927-4070-93cf-b403e75c5754", "type": "concept", "title": "Spending multiplier"}, {"id": "9e471ef8-90c2-44d5-82a2-df168dea153a", "type": "concept", "title": "Tax multiplier"}, {"id": "731c2ec1-1350-48b5-be84-85f3e642b737", "type": "concept", "title": "Crowding out and leakages"}], "description": "Multipliers explain why one dollar of spending or tax change can have a larger or smaller effect on GDP. Students learn why context matters."}, {"id": "17a98e25-b427-461d-a3dd-15bd5c026de0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Deficits and debt", "children": [{"id": "f977ffa5-3afc-4a0a-9101-325ad1467c57", "type": "concept", "title": "Budget deficit versus national debt"}, {"id": "81d75c0e-2a88-4c57-be22-ff9073b2a53c", "type": "concept", "title": "Debt-to-GDP ratio"}, {"id": "18d8fbd2-2df0-4f59-877c-2bc34de680e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Interest payments"}, {"id": "d8b0d7de-49a8-488c-87e1-f65099ea0299", "type": "concept", "title": "Primary deficit"}], "description": "Students learn how budget flows become accumulated debt. The goal is to separate short-run stabilization from long-run sustainability."}, {"id": "88cb1e23-852e-452d-8823-8a7dc2961b09", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fiscal policy evaluation", "children": [{"id": "45bec985-b07e-4374-96b9-1e5bdb50f451", "type": "concept", "title": "Recognition, implementation, and impact lags"}, {"id": "a772ad4c-b6d0-4a03-a59d-0ffa4d2b3990", "type": "concept", "title": "Distributional effects"}, {"id": "039d88c0-b4ac-4cac-800a-0bd49018be3f", "type": "concept", "title": "Supply-side effects"}, {"id": "00a0e29b-1696-46e6-bf22-de390c8e8172", "type": "concept", "title": "Debt sustainability and credibility"}], "description": "Students learn to judge fiscal policy by timing, targeting, incentives, and tradeoffs. This prepares them for real policy debates."}]}, {"id": "98524457-a2ac-4090-b560-813e99485eed", "type": "topic", "title": "Monetary Policy and Central Banks", "description": "This unit explains how central banks influence interest rates, financial conditions, inflation, and output. Students learn why money is a policy tool, not just a medium of exchange.", "children": [{"id": "c3f16e49-5b39-4a85-9dae-a5772368eb77", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Central bank roles", "children": [{"id": "46d1b8bb-63dd-4702-86dd-47aaf2cc8eee", "type": "concept", "title": "Price stability"}, {"id": "28d9fc25-af14-4717-9218-48384d60e755", "type": "concept", "title": "Maximum employment mandates"}, {"id": "173449d0-e55f-4337-bd92-a71b7b1a1b39", "type": "concept", "title": "Lender of last resort"}, {"id": "f8995e8c-9b9b-4dbd-9e52-7d2b58c9cab8", "type": "concept", "title": "Financial stability"}], "description": "Students learn what central banks do and why independence and credibility matter. The gist is that central banks manage the monetary and financial environment."}, {"id": "49c827aa-d5da-4706-87e6-c1bfa8b0b003", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Policy instruments", "children": [{"id": "24912189-b458-44d6-9620-69dfbf3464f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Policy interest rates"}, {"id": "596ad57c-9420-4fba-8dd7-827f61579374", "type": "concept", "title": "Open market operations"}, {"id": "b736c006-da1a-4a19-bba2-c0a049e77734", "type": "concept", "title": "Reserve requirements"}, {"id": "2d0c4728-f2b5-43f5-b2b1-77638bd4bbf4", "type": "concept", "title": "Discount window"}, {"id": "9441ad2a-8983-4b3a-bd1f-3aa2c2c7a013", "type": "concept", "title": "Quantitative easing"}], "description": "Students learn the tools central banks use to affect interest rates and liquidity. This connects classroom models to actual institutions."}, {"id": "fcc34206-758b-47c7-883e-44687f24725f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Monetary transmission", "children": [{"id": "bcc43bcb-7940-4276-bff1-1d1520281ddc", "type": "concept", "title": "Interest-rate channel"}, {"id": "28ba2fa5-0ceb-47cc-b044-95b1862d45c6", "type": "concept", "title": "Credit channel"}, {"id": "ff76e4de-589f-4281-bcbf-47ec8f701b5e", "type": "concept", "title": "Exchange-rate channel"}, {"id": "a2bdbcc3-3aa3-4ada-a82b-58bfc9d55f2d", "type": "concept", "title": "Asset-price channel"}, {"id": "d28c9baf-4965-48df-afb1-aa24bd3e6165", "type": "concept", "title": "Expectations channel"}], "description": "Transmission explains how a policy-rate change moves through the economy. Students learn why effects are indirect and uncertain."}, {"id": "86012301-127a-4b75-aed0-c34cee5de96d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Policy rules and judgment", "children": [{"id": "ad0c455d-9579-450d-ad9a-c2ef8ea6cbc8", "type": "concept", "title": "Taylor rule intuition"}, {"id": "00e1a777-c2d7-4f39-ae0f-bcc4f633bd22", "type": "concept", "title": "Inflation targeting"}, {"id": "0e781d85-8a25-4f25-9c9c-b6c7f21920a5", "type": "concept", "title": "Forward guidance"}, {"id": "2433287f-6f27-4d45-a749-efdaf48206b9", "type": "concept", "title": "Zero lower bound constraints"}], "description": "Students learn how central banks balance systematic rules with changing conditions. This supports analysis of inflation targeting and crisis response."}]}, {"id": "d4448ef6-5160-42d0-8500-029e114270ae", "type": "topic", "title": "Money, Banking, and Financial Markets", "description": "This unit connects macroeconomics to the financial system. Students learn how banks, money creation, credit, and interest rates shape real economic activity.", "children": [{"id": "9d45fa02-9287-4f4d-8a46-6eab028328f4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Functions and measures of money", "children": [{"id": "cd8951d6-5f72-43b9-b62c-3123ea17b86f", "type": "concept", "title": "Medium of exchange"}, {"id": "91ea3b57-e49e-4861-ad61-30e6ff7de0e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Unit of account"}, {"id": "d223a005-66db-4d41-b8a7-9a8193fca3dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Store of value"}, {"id": "fea159cf-0233-4830-a6c8-2adaa5c98056", "type": "concept", "title": "M1 and M2"}], "description": "Money lowers transaction costs and supports pricing, saving, and exchange. Students learn why economists define money in several ways."}, {"id": "2edc70e4-0d90-4746-aafc-887c3e706561", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Banks and money creation", "children": [{"id": "9692fd77-ff76-445b-9289-3788c5c85f2b", "type": "concept", "title": "Fractional reserves"}, {"id": "5cbd8c7c-3e71-490a-8211-979716d0b505", "type": "concept", "title": "Deposit creation"}, {"id": "cdcaf1e0-8c99-4145-8366-bf457cf3c436", "type": "concept", "title": "Money multiplier intuition"}, {"id": "15e38a32-25d1-4d50-a63c-d2127b827d19", "type": "concept", "title": "Bank capital and liquidity"}], "description": "Students learn how deposits and lending expand the money supply. The point is to understand banking as a balance-sheet system."}, {"id": "5f0cad5f-1ebf-4516-95c2-d89a39d6b4d6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interest rates and financial markets", "children": [{"id": "546272c9-b4d8-46e1-a66d-bf7bf33b682a", "type": "concept", "title": "Nominal interest rates"}, {"id": "fbc04514-fdab-4de5-9cec-ade2965c4d49", "type": "concept", "title": "Real interest rates"}, {"id": "4a297d82-c5db-4ea2-b105-b0f87862eb52", "type": "concept", "title": "Yield curves"}, {"id": "3f236562-c7bc-4863-bfc9-6d0a744566a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk premiums"}], "description": "Interest rates connect savers, borrowers, investors, and central banks. Students learn the difference between nominal and real rates."}, {"id": "6571e576-7b5a-45d3-9ddc-b394d0f2f483", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Financial instability", "children": [{"id": "146bb872-6fa4-4eb3-a8f9-6e80683cd7cd", "type": "concept", "title": "Leverage"}, {"id": "975c760a-aa79-4ee1-945d-54e04d7785b8", "type": "concept", "title": "Bank runs"}, {"id": "09c67f5c-d5ec-4d0f-9f5c-0e142343947b", "type": "concept", "title": "Credit crunches"}, {"id": "66d1b5fe-e420-4754-88f2-3480bc89ead0", "type": "concept", "title": "Systemic risk"}, {"id": "1f692c29-f136-4f93-815d-e47d017a9356", "type": "concept", "title": "Macroprudential regulation"}], "description": "Students learn why finance can amplify booms and downturns. This creates a bridge to recession analysis and policy response."}]}, {"id": "36388793-5ffe-4b17-8f77-3b6e18821923", "type": "topic", "title": "Long-Run Economic Growth and Productivity", "description": "This unit asks why living standards rise over decades and why some countries grow faster than others. Students learn that long-run prosperity depends on productivity, capital, technology, and institutions.", "children": [{"id": "b935a0bc-8a48-4228-ad86-bdd7f497903f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Growth measurement", "children": [{"id": "5df52a6b-a47a-4675-9fae-7b54e3926acc", "type": "concept", "title": "Real GDP per capita"}, {"id": "9161acc7-0460-4b9e-bc16-f5b4a3bf52d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Growth rates"}, {"id": "bf910e20-493e-4139-8bfc-05be41b9cea8", "type": "concept", "title": "Rule of 70"}, {"id": "ea09f47c-9c69-4693-a1a2-38da8cc40846", "type": "concept", "title": "Convergence and divergence"}], "description": "Students learn how to measure long-run improvements in living standards. The gist is that small growth-rate differences compound dramatically."}, {"id": "df05310c-2841-4c81-8c53-9846338f6276", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sources of growth", "children": [{"id": "5fa17c78-723b-4fcc-af4a-088d2817b9ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Physical capital"}, {"id": "4246916c-105e-4920-a94d-f0188429d4a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Human capital"}, {"id": "6e4627c0-e387-490b-86da-10f1608fa270", "type": "concept", "title": "Technology"}, {"id": "a7f6eaad-0d80-455e-94dc-84a58b09d445", "type": "concept", "title": "Natural resources"}, {"id": "ac7b5de3-d553-4d40-b644-ba599cf9e19f", "type": "concept", "title": "Institutions"}], "description": "Students learn the main drivers of productive capacity. This turns growth from a mystery into a set of mechanisms."}, {"id": "4c0334f2-d2aa-4ffa-a511-f07a839a61e3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Solow model intuition", "children": [{"id": "28bb12df-2d39-4abd-a4a3-34456593cc28", "type": "concept", "title": "Capital deepening"}, {"id": "9709693c-5a9a-4189-8606-883e1ee58dff", "type": "concept", "title": "Diminishing returns"}, {"id": "6644d2dd-9993-48ec-888d-eae341f1addc", "type": "concept", "title": "Steady state"}, {"id": "19a93455-57a9-40d7-84c7-cf288e3d0d9d", "type": "concept", "title": "Technological progress"}], "description": "The Solow model gives a simple framework for capital accumulation and steady-state growth. Students learn why investment alone cannot explain permanent growth."}, {"id": "1683a7c5-ff35-46d7-8ac8-8bb1032c7b5e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Productivity and policy", "children": [{"id": "a408da98-b6d5-4586-8745-7d3f965992f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Research and development"}, {"id": "23034d4f-ae85-4747-bafa-d19557202f0e", "type": "concept", "title": "Education and training"}, {"id": "2f3833ef-5548-48c5-939d-dc146d06d1bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Infrastructure"}, {"id": "8d11d23c-07f0-4dec-8e60-f76aef95c9d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Property rights and rule of law"}, {"id": "f26eebbd-57d9-4958-a7f3-ab28a18969b7", "type": "concept", "title": "Openness to trade and ideas"}], "description": "Students learn how policy can support or hinder growth. The point is to connect macro outcomes to education, infrastructure, innovation, and governance."}]}, {"id": "9ff88c17-4e2f-41e3-97c0-9244932bf8f1", "type": "topic", "title": "Business Cycles, Recessions, and Financial Crises", "description": "This unit explains short-run expansions and contractions. Students learn how to identify cycles, interpret recession indicators, and understand crisis dynamics.", "children": [{"id": "9f99897d-b30c-4a7a-8b1e-9f8c5d99a060", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Business cycle phases", "children": [{"id": "0c8c8207-2c9f-4fa0-a11d-dc8621ae5b3f", "type": "concept", "title": "Expansion"}, {"id": "9b7165af-bc9d-4f43-8083-a8e92839a837", "type": "concept", "title": "Peak"}, {"id": "730c079d-55e8-4a73-ae65-d65df1d6670b", "type": "concept", "title": "Recession"}, {"id": "fe314153-130b-41a4-9fcc-a398382a34d9", "type": "concept", "title": "Trough"}, {"id": "01716550-87c5-4f00-8eaf-8a215259beb2", "type": "concept", "title": "Recovery"}], "description": "Students learn the vocabulary of expansions, peaks, recessions, troughs, and recoveries. This provides a timeline for interpreting macro news."}, {"id": "d4c789d2-bc43-4b79-94cb-6f60627ea698", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cycle indicators", "children": [{"id": "6e18910c-c5ee-4576-bcbb-a41f9f25b244", "type": "concept", "title": "Real GDP"}, {"id": "21174861-40a0-4474-a06e-3e45190c1ea2", "type": "concept", "title": "Payroll employment"}, {"id": "74da016f-e38b-4d69-8a55-8d90b47c8369", "type": "concept", "title": "Industrial production"}, {"id": "7cc1681b-f488-41ad-b130-d3be7bb32057", "type": "concept", "title": "Retail sales"}, {"id": "185d6298-eff1-4041-ba28-ca477b46fe49", "type": "concept", "title": "Yield curve and leading indicators"}], "description": "Students learn how economists identify economic turning points. The gist is to use multiple indicators rather than one headline number."}, {"id": "4575dd61-2410-4680-9f3b-edf6c37330db", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Demand-driven recessions", "children": [{"id": "2ed72081-36a7-43c2-99f1-48c06e83495b", "type": "concept", "title": "Investment declines"}, {"id": "8e877ef4-a50e-400e-b971-1eeb7e800ea8", "type": "concept", "title": "Consumer confidence"}, {"id": "bbce3ccc-7bf2-4d35-b618-f5588acb3bbd", "type": "concept", "title": "Inventory cycles"}, {"id": "aa243104-95f0-406f-8060-2adc30e0cce5", "type": "concept", "title": "Multiplier effects"}], "description": "Students learn how drops in spending can reduce output and employment. This links recessions to AD-AS, fiscal policy, and monetary policy."}, {"id": "84c1cd70-85f1-4b50-8fc3-efb2c4815d5c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Financial crises and policy response", "children": [{"id": "2d31e7fd-ebdb-4005-8b4c-945500ab9d24", "type": "concept", "title": "Asset bubbles"}, {"id": "f79b451c-4d84-4c59-aa48-0db87cc114a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Liquidity versus solvency"}, {"id": "da2f97b2-ae4d-4bed-9b68-6c91ab7c889e", "type": "concept", "title": "Banking panics"}, {"id": "9f098f47-0a5f-45cf-9293-9dc0d8d9b2c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Lender-of-last-resort actions"}, {"id": "a5c59890-2b23-408b-b305-0b2c4065576b", "type": "concept", "title": "Fiscal and monetary emergency responses"}], "description": "Financial crises are severe because credit problems can spread across the real economy. Students learn the basic crisis mechanism and policy toolkit."}]}, {"id": "5c2053e6-5212-40b9-ad5b-3504ff185a5d", "type": "topic", "title": "International Trade, Comparative Advantage, and Capital Flows", "description": "This unit places the national economy in global context. Students learn why countries trade, why trade creates winners and losers, and how capital moves across borders.", "children": [{"id": "d52b8b6c-1621-4a9b-8017-5a3c40433e05", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Comparative advantage", "children": [{"id": "91aa6f65-1768-49cb-aade-fec01675785c", "type": "concept", "title": "Absolute advantage"}, {"id": "196d2313-5b7f-49b2-be40-f8ee6ba0afa8", "type": "concept", "title": "Opportunity cost"}, {"id": "d70824de-59a5-47b2-a7c7-20d015191934", "type": "concept", "title": "Specialization"}, {"id": "381d44b8-8eca-4a77-98d5-c643722b695d", "type": "concept", "title": "Terms of trade"}], "description": "Students learn the core logic of gains from trade. The gist is that trade can be beneficial even when one country is more productive in everything."}, {"id": "cb774323-6c2b-4f3d-a41b-ce5184050615", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Trade patterns and policy", "children": [{"id": "2f07a3be-8d18-4db6-b6e9-17af311aafe7", "type": "concept", "title": "Tariffs and quotas"}, {"id": "2b91c9a2-faba-4a79-a0ea-9ea52ad27fd8", "type": "concept", "title": "Trade agreements"}, {"id": "34e12f7f-1760-4f57-88d7-30b15059f07b", "type": "concept", "title": "Protectionism"}, {"id": "05a3b118-8445-4641-9760-1bb8c7127694", "type": "concept", "title": "Distributional effects"}], "description": "Students learn why countries export some goods and import others, and why trade policy is politically contested."}, {"id": "7413cea5-877c-4ee9-ac44-faef57bcfdf5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Capital flows", "children": [{"id": "30dcb115-06fa-49ff-a08f-594ebd682cb0", "type": "concept", "title": "Foreign direct investment"}, {"id": "86ab17c1-fd53-4b05-8679-e195ad6a3c2a", "type": "concept", "title": "Portfolio flows"}, {"id": "68f37d8f-e471-4b79-a622-6bb2d17b59a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Current account and capital account links"}, {"id": "5362af94-16a9-46a3-8692-175f4e20d8a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Sudden stops"}], "description": "Capital flows connect saving and investment across countries. Students learn how cross-border finance affects growth, risk, and exchange rates."}, {"id": "71648552-8a3a-4348-bd73-b24e196909b6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global business context", "children": [{"id": "d9f20f05-3a6d-456d-832b-a56ed2a7e4b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Global value chains"}, {"id": "1d82118e-2fd1-4a32-ae2c-0fb0db648fb6", "type": "concept", "title": "Emerging markets"}, {"id": "3c607aa8-651f-4189-9278-52285c98360e", "type": "concept", "title": "Country risk"}, {"id": "6732a22e-1cb7-488f-891f-3c47659e015d", "type": "concept", "title": "Supply-side shocks"}, {"id": "fdbe43d3-a3b2-478e-83e2-f83889396400", "type": "concept", "title": "Geopolitics and trade policy"}], "description": "MBA and supply-chain curricula point to the need for strategic global awareness. Students learn to connect macro conditions to firm decisions."}]}, {"id": "0b88dcd4-4eb5-41ec-9417-3a640ce49ada", "type": "topic", "title": "Exchange Rates, Balance of Payments, and Open-Economy Macroeconomics", "description": "The final unit explains how currencies, trade balances, and international payments interact. Students learn how open-economy conditions shape inflation, competitiveness, and policy choices.", "children": [{"id": "dfad6c33-578f-48f3-9934-8bdacfa59449", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Exchange rates", "children": [{"id": "e8e5f0ef-5fee-452d-af34-910d52a2ff17", "type": "concept", "title": "Nominal exchange rates"}, {"id": "d652088f-65b4-4c30-b03b-b62bdc437fe6", "type": "concept", "title": "Real exchange rates"}, {"id": "35a13ce5-2511-4b1d-9832-ce0dbfa42ad4", "type": "concept", "title": "Appreciation and depreciation"}, {"id": "6ed8bc05-ec80-489a-8c42-4a8c5a990287", "type": "concept", "title": "Foreign exchange markets"}], "description": "Students learn what exchange rates measure and why currency movements matter. This is essential for finance, trade, and global business decisions."}, {"id": "07443d1b-ede7-41f2-9f30-b1a736c89e3e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Balance of payments", "children": [{"id": "4ff3a7fe-bf23-4061-b011-f885cc46af79", "type": "concept", "title": "Current account"}, {"id": "3f736cde-070c-4d2b-91c2-4952dcfa6bda", "type": "concept", "title": "Capital and financial account"}, {"id": "5ed21547-6fae-4e08-92f8-cd9f29de14c6", "type": "concept", "title": "Official reserves"}, {"id": "303ad8ab-d00a-4ea3-bd47-71f1b4820dec", "type": "concept", "title": "Balance-of-payments identity"}], "description": "The balance of payments records economic transactions with the rest of the world. Students learn how trade, income, transfers, and capital flows fit together."}, {"id": "f5ded4ce-aee7-4763-a656-146ba448dd27", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Currency regimes", "children": [{"id": "69734545-ad04-4630-b642-e43c3d60d13a", "type": "concept", "title": "Floating exchange rates"}, {"id": "1495c1d9-6303-4b70-963f-2031e937fc21", "type": "concept", "title": "Fixed pegs"}, {"id": "2d3714f4-6551-4b1f-97e8-87ed749294cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Currency unions"}, {"id": "76aab5fc-51a5-4572-afba-e753b958bbe6", "type": "concept", "title": "Impossible trinity"}], "description": "Students learn how fixed, floating, and managed exchange rates change policy constraints. The gist is that no regime removes tradeoffs."}, {"id": "42ade094-6044-43e8-aa26-6acf2772c984", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Open-economy policy and risk", "children": [{"id": "fa36ec94-943c-4787-b546-8ff7ac3d35f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Exchange-rate pass-through"}, {"id": "f9fac869-7212-4c75-953c-8f9404769852", "type": "concept", "title": "Monetary policy under capital mobility"}, {"id": "56aaab8b-3060-45d3-be35-ae6df7eef619", "type": "concept", "title": "Sovereign debt and country risk"}, {"id": "e2b93038-8a76-47dd-954e-1d1c64223a29", "type": "concept", "title": "Scenario planning for global shocks"}], "description": "Students end by applying macro tools to global scenarios. The point is to analyze how policy, currency risk, and capital flows affect firms and countries."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$macrojson$::jsonb,
  true,
  false,
  'course',
  'public'
where not exists (
  select 1 from public.learning_paths where slug = 'macroeconomics'
);

update public.learning_paths
set
  title = 'Macroeconomics',
  goal = 'Macroeconomics',
  summary = 'This course follows a ten-unit sequence on national income, inflation and unemployment, aggregate demand and supply, fiscal and monetary policy, money and banking, long-run growth, business cycles, international trade, and open-economy macroeconomics.',
  data = $macrojson${"slug": "macroeconomics", "title": "Macroeconomics", "description": "This course follows a ten-unit sequence on national income, inflation and unemployment, aggregate demand and supply, fiscal and monetary policy, money and banking, long-run growth, business cycles, international trade, and open-economy macroeconomics.", "topics": [{"id": "4989cd8c-2e2d-4f5a-bd9a-0e611bef7efb", "type": "topic", "title": "National Income Accounting: GDP, GNP, GNI, and Macro Data", "description": "This unit teaches students how economists measure the size and composition of an economy. It turns broad claims about the economy into concrete, comparable indicators.", "children": [{"id": "19985e6c-9d08-4b9f-8902-33522051dea2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "GDP and output measurement", "children": [{"id": "27228acf-f7ad-4d1f-ae7a-0b6a77ab2da0", "type": "concept", "title": "Final goods and services"}, {"id": "2a58bb27-0906-43f2-9058-2fcc6201d76e", "type": "concept", "title": "Market value and production within borders"}, {"id": "3ab60089-65ee-49cd-ace2-409cdf395277", "type": "concept", "title": "Expenditure approach: C + I + G + NX"}, {"id": "9f3a8e9b-1410-4fb6-ae8d-6e3ea30e47c0", "type": "concept", "title": "Value-added approach"}], "description": "Students learn what GDP counts and why it is the central measure of production. The gist is that GDP is useful but incomplete."}, {"id": "0f50c16d-5f23-4e38-a571-65121851b20b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "GNP, GNI, and income concepts", "children": [{"id": "39023a97-8bcc-435c-b750-eba6a2acc93e", "type": "concept", "title": "Gross national product"}, {"id": "5defdd57-2ab0-4e94-b896-dee62c21f31a", "type": "concept", "title": "Gross national income"}, {"id": "51c73817-09ab-4678-8372-db4a67237f9c", "type": "concept", "title": "Net factor income from abroad"}, {"id": "a67f31af-a9a9-41c9-baf1-4298ffa4ae47", "type": "concept", "title": "Why multinational activity complicates measurement"}], "description": "These measures clarify the difference between production in a place and income earned by a country's residents. This matters for global business and cross-country comparison."}, {"id": "5dbbda53-a332-4132-ba20-eeb1b3e3bfa7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Nominal versus real values", "children": [{"id": "84fe6b95-73ab-4229-bb57-4470d5b83344", "type": "concept", "title": "Nominal GDP"}, {"id": "904abebc-5396-48de-ac52-7f921a7759b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Real GDP"}, {"id": "93b73424-0074-424c-887b-55990b56efed", "type": "concept", "title": "GDP deflator"}, {"id": "a3c72f74-d843-4dc3-b31d-f7a763330cc9", "type": "concept", "title": "Base years and index numbers"}], "description": "Students learn to separate price changes from quantity changes. This is the key to interpreting growth over time."}, {"id": "682ef01d-a67a-474d-b43a-98704f1d595e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Using macro data responsibly", "children": [{"id": "40418492-cd26-4af2-a68a-59bb32277551", "type": "concept", "title": "Per-capita measures"}, {"id": "50727d4f-3079-4f52-ae5a-2420a2a085e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Seasonal adjustment"}, {"id": "0ba052c1-3e3c-43d3-812a-a784883d6514", "type": "concept", "title": "Data revisions"}, {"id": "59e26f5e-19fa-4eb1-aa6f-306acabd72e0", "type": "concept", "title": "Limits of GDP: household work, inequality, environment, and well-being"}], "description": "Macro data are estimates built from definitions, surveys, and revisions. Students learn to read data with precision rather than false certainty."}]}, {"id": "5db4a939-790b-4f6b-8327-f867cfddd02b", "type": "topic", "title": "Inflation, CPI, Unemployment, and the Phillips Curve", "description": "This unit covers the macro indicators people feel most directly: prices and jobs. Students learn how inflation and unemployment are measured and why they create policy tradeoffs.", "children": [{"id": "49c1eec0-79f0-4022-baae-9b75ead9ab0e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inflation and price indexes", "children": [{"id": "e6a56d32-7aca-4ffa-8297-4739880ab27e", "type": "concept", "title": "Consumer Price Index"}, {"id": "db3ca5d4-448a-49ea-93f5-e0de96de83b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Producer Price Index"}, {"id": "efe181bd-dda0-4b3e-a250-7a777212f024", "type": "concept", "title": "GDP deflator"}, {"id": "21302598-9cff-4e23-a959-58625b6f4dcb", "type": "concept", "title": "Core versus headline inflation"}], "description": "Inflation measures the rate at which the general price level rises. The point is to distinguish broad inflation from changes in one price."}, {"id": "900b940d-d3f5-435e-9867-afd70beafd5e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Costs and causes of inflation", "children": [{"id": "696bb649-0d88-49f5-8c57-46a41ff2e0c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Purchasing power"}, {"id": "172953e2-6c50-4e31-a818-fd6e142ec824", "type": "concept", "title": "Menu costs and shoe-leather costs"}, {"id": "3ebb4eac-89e9-420e-abb3-7f00201a2eb8", "type": "concept", "title": "Unexpected inflation and debtors/creditors"}, {"id": "ee75b16c-750f-4676-a66a-99ed5a044023", "type": "concept", "title": "Demand-pull and cost-push inflation"}], "description": "Students learn why inflation matters even when wages and prices both change. The gist is that inflation redistributes purchasing power and can distort decisions."}, {"id": "62e7ae01-3e30-46eb-871e-f199694ae240", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Unemployment measurement", "children": [{"id": "15de7f0b-c503-403c-aeb1-989c6a2437d7", "type": "concept", "title": "Labor force"}, {"id": "e5b7fdaa-1aa2-4fc8-a32e-cd4713613036", "type": "concept", "title": "Unemployment rate"}, {"id": "3e30b7c4-4ff3-44e8-9013-fa8d5b7284f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Labor force participation"}, {"id": "e793fcd8-9e0c-4a90-989d-fea9da802b79", "type": "concept", "title": "Underemployment and discouraged workers"}], "description": "Unemployment is a labor-market indicator, but it is not as simple as counting people without jobs. Students learn the definitions behind the headline rate."}, {"id": "126055f3-332d-4124-a39a-4be9783ae09e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Phillips curve intuition", "children": [{"id": "ce9f0dfe-fb2d-4b31-973f-c0c1e2498faf", "type": "concept", "title": "Short-run Phillips curve"}, {"id": "b75e9c22-e9f3-4cbd-89c1-61589f9dc364", "type": "concept", "title": "Inflation expectations"}, {"id": "67e88280-dc78-411d-a428-1333cd27fcbd", "type": "concept", "title": "Natural rate of unemployment"}, {"id": "e8f23e89-933b-4bfa-981f-0d29e5ed6dd3", "type": "concept", "title": "Stagflation as a challenge to simple tradeoffs"}], "description": "The Phillips curve introduces the relationship between inflation and unemployment. Students learn why the short-run tradeoff can shift when expectations change."}]}, {"id": "df4887ce-6a1e-4f51-8766-fb5a81b3cd7d", "type": "topic", "title": "Aggregate Demand and Aggregate Supply", "description": "This unit gives students the main framework for analyzing economy-wide fluctuations. It shows how spending, production capacity, prices, and output interact.", "children": [{"id": "61cfe082-8a60-413e-bf16-a29a57db0b15", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Aggregate demand", "children": [{"id": "164372f4-4a67-4274-933e-22e80e3c56ef", "type": "concept", "title": "Components of AD"}, {"id": "1fee2694-2c7f-484d-b1ac-4b105cc90069", "type": "concept", "title": "Wealth effect"}, {"id": "79dd4de4-0a63-4ac9-9643-bbafa55780d2", "type": "concept", "title": "Interest-rate effect"}, {"id": "3132d52a-d59d-4e5c-b42d-7903584bf77d", "type": "concept", "title": "Exchange-rate effect"}], "description": "Aggregate demand represents planned spending across the economy. Students learn why consumption, investment, government spending, and net exports move together with the price level."}, {"id": "fca2bac8-f10c-4b76-94cb-e15e71942194", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Short-run aggregate supply", "children": [{"id": "065c5072-cee3-45b1-9191-57127ae562a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Sticky wages and prices"}, {"id": "b3dcede2-5c9b-4f53-8c89-2f4bf4f6851e", "type": "concept", "title": "Input costs"}, {"id": "c2da711b-1ddd-4232-b56a-d350ebec3010", "type": "concept", "title": "Productivity shocks"}, {"id": "58687974-8175-4350-95d1-63dd22690c5e", "type": "concept", "title": "Supply shocks"}], "description": "Short-run aggregate supply explains why output can rise or fall with prices before wages and expectations fully adjust."}, {"id": "88d50c00-4619-457c-a009-57a346cd9cc1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Long-run aggregate supply", "children": [{"id": "9b256e70-8539-4e72-8872-c3e233b3941b", "type": "concept", "title": "Potential GDP"}, {"id": "53f798dd-24e9-4879-a169-29fa928d3d6a", "type": "concept", "title": "Full-employment output"}, {"id": "86188d4d-b46b-4e00-9362-a3ce8b75c5cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Natural rate concepts"}, {"id": "9c8d239a-c48c-4da2-b550-9bd081b8df87", "type": "concept", "title": "Shifts from labor, capital, technology, and institutions"}], "description": "Long-run supply reflects productive capacity rather than short-run demand. Students learn the difference between temporary fluctuations and potential output."}, {"id": "f8c253b4-17d4-48c3-9b23-96b3637268be", "type": "subtopic", "title": "AD-AS equilibrium", "children": [{"id": "394012ca-85a2-4f0b-bfaf-ecd23148d6c2", "type": "concept", "title": "Short-run equilibrium"}, {"id": "d61121d1-a827-4580-bbc0-16f0ddb0c251", "type": "concept", "title": "Recessionary gap"}, {"id": "5d21e90e-396e-42a7-ac1c-c44acc1d57d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Inflationary gap"}, {"id": "5a0e3387-a3a8-40c3-969f-3fd252e4140d", "type": "concept", "title": "Demand shocks versus supply shocks"}], "description": "The AD-AS model connects inflation, unemployment, growth, and policy in one diagram. Students use it to reason through recessions, booms, and shocks."}]}, {"id": "e37bf733-3870-4bfd-9846-f3810938a5da", "type": "topic", "title": "Fiscal Policy and Government Budgets", "description": "Fiscal policy shows how government spending and taxation influence aggregate demand, distribution, debt, and long-run capacity. Students learn both the power and constraints of budget policy.", "children": [{"id": "b11d4ef1-256e-4353-b8c6-880333f8e115", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Government spending and taxes", "children": [{"id": "e6a3136a-cf0f-465b-bb50-10a96dd3ac80", "type": "concept", "title": "Government purchases"}, {"id": "8adb8440-f268-44c4-b59d-1499821979d3", "type": "concept", "title": "Transfers"}, {"id": "f82320db-a3eb-4512-b724-37e04072dc77", "type": "concept", "title": "Tax rates and tax bases"}, {"id": "c4b52ef5-6076-4a8e-b41e-4c5e78e08ba6", "type": "concept", "title": "Automatic stabilizers"}], "description": "Students learn the main tools of fiscal policy. The gist is that changes in spending and taxes alter demand and incentives."}, {"id": "c30f47a4-95fd-41a6-87b3-51927c8ac9cf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Multipliers", "children": [{"id": "13e0b6df-8c67-4ddc-9d11-54cbe2f76031", "type": "concept", "title": "Marginal propensity to consume"}, {"id": "616f3080-e927-4070-93cf-b403e75c5754", "type": "concept", "title": "Spending multiplier"}, {"id": "9e471ef8-90c2-44d5-82a2-df168dea153a", "type": "concept", "title": "Tax multiplier"}, {"id": "731c2ec1-1350-48b5-be84-85f3e642b737", "type": "concept", "title": "Crowding out and leakages"}], "description": "Multipliers explain why one dollar of spending or tax change can have a larger or smaller effect on GDP. Students learn why context matters."}, {"id": "17a98e25-b427-461d-a3dd-15bd5c026de0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Deficits and debt", "children": [{"id": "f977ffa5-3afc-4a0a-9101-325ad1467c57", "type": "concept", "title": "Budget deficit versus national debt"}, {"id": "81d75c0e-2a88-4c57-be22-ff9073b2a53c", "type": "concept", "title": "Debt-to-GDP ratio"}, {"id": "18d8fbd2-2df0-4f59-877c-2bc34de680e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Interest payments"}, {"id": "d8b0d7de-49a8-488c-87e1-f65099ea0299", "type": "concept", "title": "Primary deficit"}], "description": "Students learn how budget flows become accumulated debt. The goal is to separate short-run stabilization from long-run sustainability."}, {"id": "88cb1e23-852e-452d-8823-8a7dc2961b09", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fiscal policy evaluation", "children": [{"id": "45bec985-b07e-4374-96b9-1e5bdb50f451", "type": "concept", "title": "Recognition, implementation, and impact lags"}, {"id": "a772ad4c-b6d0-4a03-a59d-0ffa4d2b3990", "type": "concept", "title": "Distributional effects"}, {"id": "039d88c0-b4ac-4cac-800a-0bd49018be3f", "type": "concept", "title": "Supply-side effects"}, {"id": "00a0e29b-1696-46e6-bf22-de390c8e8172", "type": "concept", "title": "Debt sustainability and credibility"}], "description": "Students learn to judge fiscal policy by timing, targeting, incentives, and tradeoffs. This prepares them for real policy debates."}]}, {"id": "98524457-a2ac-4090-b560-813e99485eed", "type": "topic", "title": "Monetary Policy and Central Banks", "description": "This unit explains how central banks influence interest rates, financial conditions, inflation, and output. Students learn why money is a policy tool, not just a medium of exchange.", "children": [{"id": "c3f16e49-5b39-4a85-9dae-a5772368eb77", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Central bank roles", "children": [{"id": "46d1b8bb-63dd-4702-86dd-47aaf2cc8eee", "type": "concept", "title": "Price stability"}, {"id": "28d9fc25-af14-4717-9218-48384d60e755", "type": "concept", "title": "Maximum employment mandates"}, {"id": "173449d0-e55f-4337-bd92-a71b7b1a1b39", "type": "concept", "title": "Lender of last resort"}, {"id": "f8995e8c-9b9b-4dbd-9e52-7d2b58c9cab8", "type": "concept", "title": "Financial stability"}], "description": "Students learn what central banks do and why independence and credibility matter. The gist is that central banks manage the monetary and financial environment."}, {"id": "49c827aa-d5da-4706-87e6-c1bfa8b0b003", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Policy instruments", "children": [{"id": "24912189-b458-44d6-9620-69dfbf3464f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Policy interest rates"}, {"id": "596ad57c-9420-4fba-8dd7-827f61579374", "type": "concept", "title": "Open market operations"}, {"id": "b736c006-da1a-4a19-bba2-c0a049e77734", "type": "concept", "title": "Reserve requirements"}, {"id": "2d0c4728-f2b5-43f5-b2b1-77638bd4bbf4", "type": "concept", "title": "Discount window"}, {"id": "9441ad2a-8983-4b3a-bd1f-3aa2c2c7a013", "type": "concept", "title": "Quantitative easing"}], "description": "Students learn the tools central banks use to affect interest rates and liquidity. This connects classroom models to actual institutions."}, {"id": "fcc34206-758b-47c7-883e-44687f24725f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Monetary transmission", "children": [{"id": "bcc43bcb-7940-4276-bff1-1d1520281ddc", "type": "concept", "title": "Interest-rate channel"}, {"id": "28ba2fa5-0ceb-47cc-b044-95b1862d45c6", "type": "concept", "title": "Credit channel"}, {"id": "ff76e4de-589f-4281-bcbf-47ec8f701b5e", "type": "concept", "title": "Exchange-rate channel"}, {"id": "a2bdbcc3-3aa3-4ada-a82b-58bfc9d55f2d", "type": "concept", "title": "Asset-price channel"}, {"id": "d28c9baf-4965-48df-afb1-aa24bd3e6165", "type": "concept", "title": "Expectations channel"}], "description": "Transmission explains how a policy-rate change moves through the economy. Students learn why effects are indirect and uncertain."}, {"id": "86012301-127a-4b75-aed0-c34cee5de96d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Policy rules and judgment", "children": [{"id": "ad0c455d-9579-450d-ad9a-c2ef8ea6cbc8", "type": "concept", "title": "Taylor rule intuition"}, {"id": "00e1a777-c2d7-4f39-ae0f-bcc4f633bd22", "type": "concept", "title": "Inflation targeting"}, {"id": "0e781d85-8a25-4f25-9c9c-b6c7f21920a5", "type": "concept", "title": "Forward guidance"}, {"id": "2433287f-6f27-4d45-a749-efdaf48206b9", "type": "concept", "title": "Zero lower bound constraints"}], "description": "Students learn how central banks balance systematic rules with changing conditions. This supports analysis of inflation targeting and crisis response."}]}, {"id": "d4448ef6-5160-42d0-8500-029e114270ae", "type": "topic", "title": "Money, Banking, and Financial Markets", "description": "This unit connects macroeconomics to the financial system. Students learn how banks, money creation, credit, and interest rates shape real economic activity.", "children": [{"id": "9d45fa02-9287-4f4d-8a46-6eab028328f4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Functions and measures of money", "children": [{"id": "cd8951d6-5f72-43b9-b62c-3123ea17b86f", "type": "concept", "title": "Medium of exchange"}, {"id": "91ea3b57-e49e-4861-ad61-30e6ff7de0e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Unit of account"}, {"id": "d223a005-66db-4d41-b8a7-9a8193fca3dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Store of value"}, {"id": "fea159cf-0233-4830-a6c8-2adaa5c98056", "type": "concept", "title": "M1 and M2"}], "description": "Money lowers transaction costs and supports pricing, saving, and exchange. Students learn why economists define money in several ways."}, {"id": "2edc70e4-0d90-4746-aafc-887c3e706561", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Banks and money creation", "children": [{"id": "9692fd77-ff76-445b-9289-3788c5c85f2b", "type": "concept", "title": "Fractional reserves"}, {"id": "5cbd8c7c-3e71-490a-8211-979716d0b505", "type": "concept", "title": "Deposit creation"}, {"id": "cdcaf1e0-8c99-4145-8366-bf457cf3c436", "type": "concept", "title": "Money multiplier intuition"}, {"id": "15e38a32-25d1-4d50-a63c-d2127b827d19", "type": "concept", "title": "Bank capital and liquidity"}], "description": "Students learn how deposits and lending expand the money supply. The point is to understand banking as a balance-sheet system."}, {"id": "5f0cad5f-1ebf-4516-95c2-d89a39d6b4d6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interest rates and financial markets", "children": [{"id": "546272c9-b4d8-46e1-a66d-bf7bf33b682a", "type": "concept", "title": "Nominal interest rates"}, {"id": "fbc04514-fdab-4de5-9cec-ade2965c4d49", "type": "concept", "title": "Real interest rates"}, {"id": "4a297d82-c5db-4ea2-b105-b0f87862eb52", "type": "concept", "title": "Yield curves"}, {"id": "3f236562-c7bc-4863-bfc9-6d0a744566a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk premiums"}], "description": "Interest rates connect savers, borrowers, investors, and central banks. Students learn the difference between nominal and real rates."}, {"id": "6571e576-7b5a-45d3-9ddc-b394d0f2f483", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Financial instability", "children": [{"id": "146bb872-6fa4-4eb3-a8f9-6e80683cd7cd", "type": "concept", "title": "Leverage"}, {"id": "975c760a-aa79-4ee1-945d-54e04d7785b8", "type": "concept", "title": "Bank runs"}, {"id": "09c67f5c-d5ec-4d0f-9f5c-0e142343947b", "type": "concept", "title": "Credit crunches"}, {"id": "66d1b5fe-e420-4754-88f2-3480bc89ead0", "type": "concept", "title": "Systemic risk"}, {"id": "1f692c29-f136-4f93-815d-e47d017a9356", "type": "concept", "title": "Macroprudential regulation"}], "description": "Students learn why finance can amplify booms and downturns. This creates a bridge to recession analysis and policy response."}]}, {"id": "36388793-5ffe-4b17-8f77-3b6e18821923", "type": "topic", "title": "Long-Run Economic Growth and Productivity", "description": "This unit asks why living standards rise over decades and why some countries grow faster than others. Students learn that long-run prosperity depends on productivity, capital, technology, and institutions.", "children": [{"id": "b935a0bc-8a48-4228-ad86-bdd7f497903f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Growth measurement", "children": [{"id": "5df52a6b-a47a-4675-9fae-7b54e3926acc", "type": "concept", "title": "Real GDP per capita"}, {"id": "9161acc7-0460-4b9e-bc16-f5b4a3bf52d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Growth rates"}, {"id": "bf910e20-493e-4139-8bfc-05be41b9cea8", "type": "concept", "title": "Rule of 70"}, {"id": "ea09f47c-9c69-4693-a1a2-38da8cc40846", "type": "concept", "title": "Convergence and divergence"}], "description": "Students learn how to measure long-run improvements in living standards. The gist is that small growth-rate differences compound dramatically."}, {"id": "df05310c-2841-4c81-8c53-9846338f6276", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sources of growth", "children": [{"id": "5fa17c78-723b-4fcc-af4a-088d2817b9ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Physical capital"}, {"id": "4246916c-105e-4920-a94d-f0188429d4a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Human capital"}, {"id": "6e4627c0-e387-490b-86da-10f1608fa270", "type": "concept", "title": "Technology"}, {"id": "a7f6eaad-0d80-455e-94dc-84a58b09d445", "type": "concept", "title": "Natural resources"}, {"id": "ac7b5de3-d553-4d40-b644-ba599cf9e19f", "type": "concept", "title": "Institutions"}], "description": "Students learn the main drivers of productive capacity. This turns growth from a mystery into a set of mechanisms."}, {"id": "4c0334f2-d2aa-4ffa-a511-f07a839a61e3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Solow model intuition", "children": [{"id": "28bb12df-2d39-4abd-a4a3-34456593cc28", "type": "concept", "title": "Capital deepening"}, {"id": "9709693c-5a9a-4189-8606-883e1ee58dff", "type": "concept", "title": "Diminishing returns"}, {"id": "6644d2dd-9993-48ec-888d-eae341f1addc", "type": "concept", "title": "Steady state"}, {"id": "19a93455-57a9-40d7-84c7-cf288e3d0d9d", "type": "concept", "title": "Technological progress"}], "description": "The Solow model gives a simple framework for capital accumulation and steady-state growth. Students learn why investment alone cannot explain permanent growth."}, {"id": "1683a7c5-ff35-46d7-8ac8-8bb1032c7b5e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Productivity and policy", "children": [{"id": "a408da98-b6d5-4586-8745-7d3f965992f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Research and development"}, {"id": "23034d4f-ae85-4747-bafa-d19557202f0e", "type": "concept", "title": "Education and training"}, {"id": "2f3833ef-5548-48c5-939d-dc146d06d1bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Infrastructure"}, {"id": "8d11d23c-07f0-4dec-8e60-f76aef95c9d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Property rights and rule of law"}, {"id": "f26eebbd-57d9-4958-a7f3-ab28a18969b7", "type": "concept", "title": "Openness to trade and ideas"}], "description": "Students learn how policy can support or hinder growth. The point is to connect macro outcomes to education, infrastructure, innovation, and governance."}]}, {"id": "9ff88c17-4e2f-41e3-97c0-9244932bf8f1", "type": "topic", "title": "Business Cycles, Recessions, and Financial Crises", "description": "This unit explains short-run expansions and contractions. Students learn how to identify cycles, interpret recession indicators, and understand crisis dynamics.", "children": [{"id": "9f99897d-b30c-4a7a-8b1e-9f8c5d99a060", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Business cycle phases", "children": [{"id": "0c8c8207-2c9f-4fa0-a11d-dc8621ae5b3f", "type": "concept", "title": "Expansion"}, {"id": "9b7165af-bc9d-4f43-8083-a8e92839a837", "type": "concept", "title": "Peak"}, {"id": "730c079d-55e8-4a73-ae65-d65df1d6670b", "type": "concept", "title": "Recession"}, {"id": "fe314153-130b-41a4-9fcc-a398382a34d9", "type": "concept", "title": "Trough"}, {"id": "01716550-87c5-4f00-8eaf-8a215259beb2", "type": "concept", "title": "Recovery"}], "description": "Students learn the vocabulary of expansions, peaks, recessions, troughs, and recoveries. This provides a timeline for interpreting macro news."}, {"id": "d4c789d2-bc43-4b79-94cb-6f60627ea698", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cycle indicators", "children": [{"id": "6e18910c-c5ee-4576-bcbb-a41f9f25b244", "type": "concept", "title": "Real GDP"}, {"id": "21174861-40a0-4474-a06e-3e45190c1ea2", "type": "concept", "title": "Payroll employment"}, {"id": "74da016f-e38b-4d69-8a55-8d90b47c8369", "type": "concept", "title": "Industrial production"}, {"id": "7cc1681b-f488-41ad-b130-d3be7bb32057", "type": "concept", "title": "Retail sales"}, {"id": "185d6298-eff1-4041-ba28-ca477b46fe49", "type": "concept", "title": "Yield curve and leading indicators"}], "description": "Students learn how economists identify economic turning points. The gist is to use multiple indicators rather than one headline number."}, {"id": "4575dd61-2410-4680-9f3b-edf6c37330db", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Demand-driven recessions", "children": [{"id": "2ed72081-36a7-43c2-99f1-48c06e83495b", "type": "concept", "title": "Investment declines"}, {"id": "8e877ef4-a50e-400e-b971-1eeb7e800ea8", "type": "concept", "title": "Consumer confidence"}, {"id": "bbce3ccc-7bf2-4d35-b618-f5588acb3bbd", "type": "concept", "title": "Inventory cycles"}, {"id": "aa243104-95f0-406f-8060-2adc30e0cce5", "type": "concept", "title": "Multiplier effects"}], "description": "Students learn how drops in spending can reduce output and employment. This links recessions to AD-AS, fiscal policy, and monetary policy."}, {"id": "84c1cd70-85f1-4b50-8fc3-efb2c4815d5c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Financial crises and policy response", "children": [{"id": "2d31e7fd-ebdb-4005-8b4c-945500ab9d24", "type": "concept", "title": "Asset bubbles"}, {"id": "f79b451c-4d84-4c59-aa48-0db87cc114a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Liquidity versus solvency"}, {"id": "da2f97b2-ae4d-4bed-9b68-6c91ab7c889e", "type": "concept", "title": "Banking panics"}, {"id": "9f098f47-0a5f-45cf-9293-9dc0d8d9b2c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Lender-of-last-resort actions"}, {"id": "a5c59890-2b23-408b-b305-0b2c4065576b", "type": "concept", "title": "Fiscal and monetary emergency responses"}], "description": "Financial crises are severe because credit problems can spread across the real economy. Students learn the basic crisis mechanism and policy toolkit."}]}, {"id": "5c2053e6-5212-40b9-ad5b-3504ff185a5d", "type": "topic", "title": "International Trade, Comparative Advantage, and Capital Flows", "description": "This unit places the national economy in global context. Students learn why countries trade, why trade creates winners and losers, and how capital moves across borders.", "children": [{"id": "d52b8b6c-1621-4a9b-8017-5a3c40433e05", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Comparative advantage", "children": [{"id": "91aa6f65-1768-49cb-aade-fec01675785c", "type": "concept", "title": "Absolute advantage"}, {"id": "196d2313-5b7f-49b2-be40-f8ee6ba0afa8", "type": "concept", "title": "Opportunity cost"}, {"id": "d70824de-59a5-47b2-a7c7-20d015191934", "type": "concept", "title": "Specialization"}, {"id": "381d44b8-8eca-4a77-98d5-c643722b695d", "type": "concept", "title": "Terms of trade"}], "description": "Students learn the core logic of gains from trade. The gist is that trade can be beneficial even when one country is more productive in everything."}, {"id": "cb774323-6c2b-4f3d-a41b-ce5184050615", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Trade patterns and policy", "children": [{"id": "2f07a3be-8d18-4db6-b6e9-17af311aafe7", "type": "concept", "title": "Tariffs and quotas"}, {"id": "2b91c9a2-faba-4a79-a0ea-9ea52ad27fd8", "type": "concept", "title": "Trade agreements"}, {"id": "34e12f7f-1760-4f57-88d7-30b15059f07b", "type": "concept", "title": "Protectionism"}, {"id": "05a3b118-8445-4641-9760-1bb8c7127694", "type": "concept", "title": "Distributional effects"}], "description": "Students learn why countries export some goods and import others, and why trade policy is politically contested."}, {"id": "7413cea5-877c-4ee9-ac44-faef57bcfdf5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Capital flows", "children": [{"id": "30dcb115-06fa-49ff-a08f-594ebd682cb0", "type": "concept", "title": "Foreign direct investment"}, {"id": "86ab17c1-fd53-4b05-8679-e195ad6a3c2a", "type": "concept", "title": "Portfolio flows"}, {"id": "68f37d8f-e471-4b79-a622-6bb2d17b59a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Current account and capital account links"}, {"id": "5362af94-16a9-46a3-8692-175f4e20d8a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Sudden stops"}], "description": "Capital flows connect saving and investment across countries. Students learn how cross-border finance affects growth, risk, and exchange rates."}, {"id": "71648552-8a3a-4348-bd73-b24e196909b6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global business context", "children": [{"id": "d9f20f05-3a6d-456d-832b-a56ed2a7e4b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Global value chains"}, {"id": "1d82118e-2fd1-4a32-ae2c-0fb0db648fb6", "type": "concept", "title": "Emerging markets"}, {"id": "3c607aa8-651f-4189-9278-52285c98360e", "type": "concept", "title": "Country risk"}, {"id": "6732a22e-1cb7-488f-891f-3c47659e015d", "type": "concept", "title": "Supply-side shocks"}, {"id": "fdbe43d3-a3b2-478e-83e2-f83889396400", "type": "concept", "title": "Geopolitics and trade policy"}], "description": "MBA and supply-chain curricula point to the need for strategic global awareness. Students learn to connect macro conditions to firm decisions."}]}, {"id": "0b88dcd4-4eb5-41ec-9417-3a640ce49ada", "type": "topic", "title": "Exchange Rates, Balance of Payments, and Open-Economy Macroeconomics", "description": "The final unit explains how currencies, trade balances, and international payments interact. Students learn how open-economy conditions shape inflation, competitiveness, and policy choices.", "children": [{"id": "dfad6c33-578f-48f3-9934-8bdacfa59449", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Exchange rates", "children": [{"id": "e8e5f0ef-5fee-452d-af34-910d52a2ff17", "type": "concept", "title": "Nominal exchange rates"}, {"id": "d652088f-65b4-4c30-b03b-b62bdc437fe6", "type": "concept", "title": "Real exchange rates"}, {"id": "35a13ce5-2511-4b1d-9832-ce0dbfa42ad4", "type": "concept", "title": "Appreciation and depreciation"}, {"id": "6ed8bc05-ec80-489a-8c42-4a8c5a990287", "type": "concept", "title": "Foreign exchange markets"}], "description": "Students learn what exchange rates measure and why currency movements matter. This is essential for finance, trade, and global business decisions."}, {"id": "07443d1b-ede7-41f2-9f30-b1a736c89e3e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Balance of payments", "children": [{"id": "4ff3a7fe-bf23-4061-b011-f885cc46af79", "type": "concept", "title": "Current account"}, {"id": "3f736cde-070c-4d2b-91c2-4952dcfa6bda", "type": "concept", "title": "Capital and financial account"}, {"id": "5ed21547-6fae-4e08-92f8-cd9f29de14c6", "type": "concept", "title": "Official reserves"}, {"id": "303ad8ab-d00a-4ea3-bd47-71f1b4820dec", "type": "concept", "title": "Balance-of-payments identity"}], "description": "The balance of payments records economic transactions with the rest of the world. Students learn how trade, income, transfers, and capital flows fit together."}, {"id": "f5ded4ce-aee7-4763-a656-146ba448dd27", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Currency regimes", "children": [{"id": "69734545-ad04-4630-b642-e43c3d60d13a", "type": "concept", "title": "Floating exchange rates"}, {"id": "1495c1d9-6303-4b70-963f-2031e937fc21", "type": "concept", "title": "Fixed pegs"}, {"id": "2d3714f4-6551-4b1f-97e8-87ed749294cb", "type": "concept", "title": "Currency unions"}, {"id": "76aab5fc-51a5-4572-afba-e753b958bbe6", "type": "concept", "title": "Impossible trinity"}], "description": "Students learn how fixed, floating, and managed exchange rates change policy constraints. The gist is that no regime removes tradeoffs."}, {"id": "42ade094-6044-43e8-aa26-6acf2772c984", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Open-economy policy and risk", "children": [{"id": "fa36ec94-943c-4787-b546-8ff7ac3d35f2", "type": "concept", "title": "Exchange-rate pass-through"}, {"id": "f9fac869-7212-4c75-953c-8f9404769852", "type": "concept", "title": "Monetary policy under capital mobility"}, {"id": "56aaab8b-3060-45d3-be35-ae6df7eef619", "type": "concept", "title": "Sovereign debt and country risk"}, {"id": "e2b93038-8a76-47dd-954e-1d1c64223a29", "type": "concept", "title": "Scenario planning for global shocks"}], "description": "Students end by applying macro tools to global scenarios. The point is to analyze how policy, currency risk, and capital flows affect firms and countries."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$macrojson$::jsonb,
